<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amadeus Aba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1311">1311</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Amade Aba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amadeus Aba was a Hungarian baron of the Aba kindred and one of the great oligarchs who ruled provinces almost independently around 1300. From the 1290s he controlled much of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, including the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> (Košice), and served several times as palatine. He was killed in Kassa in 1311, and King Charles I defeated his sons at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rozgony">Battle of Rozgony</a> in 1312.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amadeus-aba.jpg" alt="Amadeus Aba" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Szilágyi Sándor (1827–1899) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pe%C4%8Da%C5%A5_palat%C3%ADna_Omodeja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
